      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T20:11:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this method and `readData` use `ssize_t` (https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/system_data_types.7.html) to be able to report errors? How are they currently reported?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 138,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 138,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "63ab1465f8c6b6b4d727a50b167d2dc534b30af4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bdfe836a_75adc8d4",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/include/core-impl/DevicePortProxy.h",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1150374
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T23:20:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "readData and writeData are calling respective functions of BluetoothAudioSessionControl that return size_t. They are return always numbers of bytes read or written. Fails will return default init value 0.",
      "parentUuid": "98dc608a_4bcce412",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 138,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 138,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "63ab1465f8c6b6b4d727a50b167d2dc534b30af4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "611da028_4b317608",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/include/core-impl/StreamBluetooth.h",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 73,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T20:11:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since there are two locks here, we need to specify whether it\u0027s allowed to hold both of them at the same time, and in case it\u0027s allowed, state the order of acquisition. Otherwise it\u0027s easy to end up with a deadlock between two fragments of code that attempt taking these locks in different order.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "63ab1465f8c6b6b4d727a50b167d2dc534b30af4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4cb90fc0_5eac009e",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/include/core-impl/StreamBluetooth.h",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 73,
      "author": {
        "id": 1150374
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T23:47:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "mListLock as commented is meant for maintaining vectors mConnectedDevices, mBtDeviceProxies. They are initialized during the init call and all other functions of StreamBluetooth read from them. \n\nElements of mBtDeviceProxies are the actual placeholders that interact with BluetoothAudioSessionControl. While accessing them i am locking mStreamLock. With this lock held, calls to read, write, start, stop, ... are made, making the DevicePortProxy handle and its elements thread safe.",
      "parentUuid": "611da028_4b317608",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "63ab1465f8c6b6b4d727a50b167d2dc534b30af4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47c99678_790fd6f7",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/include/core-impl/StreamBluetooth.h",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 73,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-22T00:16:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the explanation! Is this correct that `mListLock` and `mStreamLock` must never be held together by the same thread? This should be documented, that\u0027s what I was asking. Unfortunately, it\u0027s not easy to express this with annotations, but at least there must be a comment about this. Although, if you are agree with the next CL comment, then this will become redundant.",
      "parentUuid": "4cb90fc0_5eac009e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "63ab1465f8c6b6b4d727a50b167d2dc534b30af4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a13cfc4e_152d44eb",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/include/core-impl/StreamBluetooth.h",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T20:11:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another issue is that it\u0027s unclear which data elements this lock actually protects. These need to be marked with `GUARDED_BY`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 74,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 74,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "63ab1465f8c6b6b4d727a50b167d2dc534b30af4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a3bd784_2bbbe651",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/include/core-impl/StreamBluetooth.h",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 1150374
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T23:47:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "mBtDevicePortProxy contains instances for each connected device that interact with BluetoothAudioSessionControl to start, stop, read and write, ...\n\nThis lock as held while making calls to DevicePortProxy, It is protecting threads from interacting with BluetoothAudioSessionControl with out locking. that is start, suspend, close, transfer are thread safe.",
      "parentUuid": "a13cfc4e_152d44eb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 74,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 74,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "63ab1465f8c6b6b4d727a50b167d2dc534b30af4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4eaa34b8_e69a6bd2",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/include/core-impl/StreamBluetooth.h",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-22T00:16:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if we make `BluetoothAudioPortAidl` thread-safe instead, since we own it? As the lock will be concealed within that class, the code will look more clear. I don\u0027t think it\u0027s a problem if we use a lock per port instead of a global lock for all ports. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "9a3bd784_2bbbe651",
